[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Philidor Defense: Légal Trap"]
[ECO "C41"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "trap,pin,mate-threat"]
[Themes "legal-mate,poisoned-queen"]
[Kind "against-us"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 d6?! { Playable, but the quiet 3...d6 invites a pin with ...Bg4, and that is how Légal's mate happens. We play 3...Bc5 instead. } 4. Nc3 4... Bg4?! { Pins the knight on f3 to the queen. Pinning against Nc3 and Bc4 allows a famous trick. } 5. Nxe5! { White leaves the queen en prise on purpose. } 5... Bxd1?? { Taking the queen is the losing mistake. If Black simply takes the knight on e5 first, White is the one in trouble. } 6. Bxf7+ { Check! The bishop attacks the king. } 6... Ke7 7. Nd5# *
